// The house the game builds today, as a blueprint. Like the game, it
// picks per house a size, one or two storeys, a roof (gable, fronted,
// hipped or saltbox), a wall (plaster, ochre, whitewash, stone or timber
// framed), a pitch, and the side its door and chimney go to: each is an
// input of "house" that varies per house. A style is kept by culling
// every part that is not of it. "two_slopes" and "hip_roof" lay the
// game's tiles; "door" and "window" are its door and windows. Written by
// a script from the game's house; the garden, the verge, the lantern and
// a hall's tower are not in it yet.
